  "control": "The same procedure run with the executor of the previous pin, the Ptah v0.23.0 release image, reproduced every checked-in reading record for record, the PostgreSQL 18 and 16 witnesses included, and all four saved exclusion plans byte for byte. The v0.26.0 image reproduced both migration History readings, the PostgreSQL restored-history refusal and both saved MySQL exclusion plans, and changed every schema reading. Each PostgreSQL schema command reads the inherit and set options of a role membership (stokaro/ptah#5884), asks whether the role it runs as is a superuser where it asked only the role's name (stokaro/ptah#5896), reads which foreign tables keep an extension's foreign-data wrapper in use (stokaro/ptah#5898), lists the aggregates, collations, foreign tables, event triggers and publications it does not compare (stokaro/ptah#5908), and reads each trigger's arguments (stokaro/ptah#5986). Each MySQL schema command reads a view's SQL SECURITY (stokaro/ptah#5902), and the refused MySQL restored-history Apply creates its revision table as utf8mb4 (stokaro/ptah#5874). The allowed Apply executes the same statements as before. The two saved PostgreSQL exclusion plans carry the same statements under new fingerprints and plan names.",
